Turn completed.
1. Root cause: the NaN/garbage path was the small-`M` runtime activation bridge, not the aligned-plan fix. In [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp), `RuntimeNvfp4PackOptions()` was selecting `swizzled_8x4` for `M<=32`. A new real-sized `M=1, K=5376, N=4096` repro in [nvfp4_gemm_runner_test.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/testing/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner_test.cpp) showed the cuBLASLt fastpath staying finite but diverging badly from the reference (`max_abs_diff=3.42723`). Forcing `swizzled_128x4` made that repro pass.

2. What I fixed: I changed the runtime fastpath in [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp) to force the validated `128x4` activation scale layout for now, leaving generic `8x4` packing support intact but disabled on the cuBLASLt bridge. I also added regression coverage in [nvfp4_gemm_runner_test.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/testing/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner_test.cpp) and [linear_op_test.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/testing/backend/linear_op_test.cpp), and updated [PLAN.md](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/proj-2026-04-01-1534/PLAN.md) to put step 1 back in progress with the new checkpoint note.

3. Compile and unit test status: passed.
- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4`
- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nvfp4_gemm_runner_test device_nvfp4_matrix_test linear_op_test -j4`
- `ctest --test-dir build-phase1-tests -R 'nvfp4_gemm_runner_test|device_nvfp4_matrix_test|linear_op_test' --output-on-failure`

4. Remaining concerns: this is a correctness-preserving workaround, not a true `8x4` backend fix. The relinked real-model smoke no longer fast-fails in the first expert layer, and a timed debug run got through layer 9 with `swizzled_128x4`, but I did not complete a full smoke/parity run to final pass/fail in this checkpoint.

CHECKPOINT: 1
